Formats re-implemented from the creators' code
============================================

Each adapter re-implements its creator's prompt format and decision head. Prompt and numerical checks against
the creator's code are recorded separately in docs/models.md, docs/accuracy.md and references/; some builds have
only prompt verification or experimental numerical coverage. No code from a model repository
is imported or run by ippon.

- Perplexity pplx-decider (src/ippon/adapters/perplexity.py): the chunked joint readout protocol of the
  pplx_decider package in perplexity-ai's model repositories (source/src/pplx_decider), Apache License 2.0.
- Cloudflare Clef and Clef-Flash (src/ippon/adapters/clef.py): the prompt and the joint schema head of
  Cloudflare's joint_schema_model.py, Apache License 2.0.
- Liquid AI d1-2B and d1-Omni-2B (src/ippon/adapters/d1.py, src/ippon/arch/lfm3.py, src/ippon/media/lfm3.py,
  src/ippon/media/lfm3_audio.py): the prompts, the set attention and the readout of Liquid AI's prompt.py,
  attention.py, runner.py, api.py and calibration.py, the LFM3 layers of modeling_lfm3.py, the picture cap, vision
  tower and projector of media.py and modeling_lfm3_vl.py, and the clip reading and resampler, log-mel front end,
  speech encoder and projector of media.py, feature_extraction_lfm3_omni.py and modeling_lfm3_omni.py, LFM Open
  License v1.0.
- Qwen3.5's image processing, vision tower and multimodal RoPE positions (src/ippon/media/qwen.py), which
  Perplexity's pplx-decider flash and Cloudflare's Clef-Flash read images through: reimplemented from Hugging Face
  transformers' Qwen2VLImageProcessor, Qwen3_5VisionModel and get_rope_index, Apache License 2.0.
- vllm-sr d3 (src/ippon/adapters/d3.py): the prompt and code readout of vllm-sr's d3_runtime and d3_format,
  Apache License 2.0.
- Torchcast Decision (src/ippon/adapters/torchcast.py, src/ippon/rounds.py): the prompt (render.py, format
  jev_render_v3), its cut to the prompt budget, its rounds for a wide choice (model.py) and the letter readout of
  Torchcast AI's torchcast_decision serving package, Apache License 2.0.
- H2O.ai H2O-Lightning (src/ippon/adapters/h2o.py, h2o_select.py): the prompt, labels, temperatures, yes/no floor,
  answers and long-record fitting of the h2o_lightning_shim.py server, its passage selection (selector_v2.py) and
  serve_config.json in H2O.ai's model repository, Apache License 2.0.
- AutoTrust Decider Mini 9B (src/ippon/adapters/autotrust.py): the prompt, slot ranges, decision head and per-kind temperatures of
  the model card's System 1 code (transformers + peft), and how its server writes a state
  (vl/serve_decide.py, `_parts`), in AutoTrust's model repository, Apache License 2.0.
- Sqwish Kettei Core and Dot (src/ippon/adapters/kettei.py, kettei_labels.json): the prompt, labels and answers of
  the sqwishai SDK's local runtime (sqwishai.kettei: _prompt.py, _request.py, alphabets.json), Apache License 2.0,
  for the models under the Kettei Community Model License 1.0.
- Base Labs elephant-1 (src/ippon/adapters/elephant.py): the prompt, block attention and slot readout of OneJev's qev
  serving runtime with the checkpoint's serve.patch (prompt.py, engine.py, readout.py, answers.py), Apache License
  2.0, for the MIT-licensed model.
- Ollama's MLX cache layout (manifests, blobs, tensor companion names and quant_type metadata)
  (src/ippon/ollama.py, quant.py): reimplemented from
  ollama/ollama's manifest and mlxrunner/model packages (https://github.com/ollama/ollama), MIT License; no Ollama
  code is included or run by the library.
- The GGUF format and llama.cpp's conversion (src/ippon/gguf/): the file layout, ggml's block formats and the
  converter's tensor names and transforms, written from llama.cpp and its gguf-py (MIT License); no llama.cpp code
  is included.

The models' weights are not distributed with ippon; each keeps its creator's licence.

Test references
===============

tests/*_numpy.py are independent numpy implementations of the architectures, written from Hugging Face
transformers' modeling files (Apache License 2.0) to check ippon's MLX ones; tests/lfm3_numpy.py from Liquid AI's
modeling_lfm3.py and attention.py (LFM Open License v1.0).
